<%#
  The Mashup explainer video. No locals.

  The <iframe> is a verbatim carry-over from the pre-redesign About page: same
  video, same accessible name, same permissions. It is the one element the owner
  asked to keep through the redesign, so it is preserved rather than modernised,
  and a test pins its source, title and lazy loading. Only its frame changed,
  from a slate border to the token palette.

  The lead-in and the link are new. The video used to sit with no context and no
  way onward; the three mashups it names are the three /mashup actually renders.
%>
<section class="about-video">
  <h2 class="about-heading">What does Mashup mean?</h2>
  <p class="about-video__lead">
    The Mashups page pairs our products with a store map, a currency converter,
    and a password checker — this is the idea they are built on.
  </p>
  <div class="about-video__frame">
    <iframe
      src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZRcP2CZ8DS8"
      title="What does Mashup mean?"
      allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
      referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
      loading="lazy"
      allowfullscreen></iframe>
  </div>
  <a href="/mashup" class="about-video__link">
    See the Mashups
  </a>
</section>
